# Kavacha patch 0054 — research continuity: branch lineage, pinned fidelity,
# compare/discard, and step-through replay (REMAINING_WORK.md §3 "Research
# continuity", closing all four open items from patch 0020).
#
# 1. BRANCH TREE IN THE SWITCHER. Patch 0020 wrote parentSpaceId onto every
#    branched Space and NOTHING EVER READ IT. "Research / branch / branch" was
#    three unrelated-looking buttons in the strip. ZenSpaceIcons now stamps a
#    clamped kavacha-branch-depth and the tooltip names the parent. It is a
#    marker, not an indent, deliberately: the strip is a fixed-size run of equal
#    buttons and indenting one breaks its alignment in both orientations. The
#    depth walk carries a visited set — a hand-edited or corrupted session file
#    could contain a parent cycle and this runs on every strip render.
#
# 2. PINNED FIDELITY. 0019 always captured `pinned` in the snapshot payload and
#    0020 always ignored it, so every branch came back with the user's pinned
#    working set demoted into the ordinary strip. Pinning happens AFTER
#    moveTabToWorkspace: pinning re-parents the tab into the pinned container,
#    and doing it first leaves the move fighting for the same element.
#
# 3. COMPARE / DISCARD. Branching is cheap by design, which is exactly why a
#    pile of branches becomes unreadable. Compare is read-only and diffs the
#    LIVE tabs of branch and parent — not the branch-point snapshot — because
#    the useful question is "how does this differ from what I'd have if I'd
#    stayed", and that is the parent as it is now. Discard is the only
#    destructive action in this patch: it confirms, it names the Space, and it
#    refuses outright on a Space with no parent, so it can never become a
#    second, softer-sounding way to delete somebody's actual work. Snapshots
#    survive a discard, so a discarded branch can be branched again.
#
# 4. STEP-THROUGH REPLAY. The timeline list answers "when were the moments";
#    replay answers "what was I looking at THEN", which is the question the
#    feature exists for and the one a column of timestamps and tab counts
#    cannot answer. Stepping is READ-ONLY — it reads one snapshot's payload and
#    lists its tabs. Restore stays non-destructive in both modes: it forks a
#    branch, so the present is never overwritten. Replay starts at the OLDEST
#    snapshot so stepping forward runs the way the work actually happened, and
#    is offered only when there are two moments to step between.
#
# Why a patch: all four touch nsZenWorkspaces internals and Zen's popupset.
#
# Touches: src/zen/spaces/ZenSpaceManager.mjs, src/zen/spaces/ZenSpaceIcons.mjs,
#          src/browser/base/content/zen-panels/popups.inc,
#          src/zen/common/styles/kavacha-spaces.inc.css (new) + zen-theme.css,
#          src/zen/common/sys/KavachaCommandRegistry.sys.mjs,
#          locales/en-US/browser/browser/zen-workspaces.ftl,
#          locales/en-US/browser/browser/zen-command-palette.ftl.
# Applies on top of 0053.
